      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1016,
          "quote":"A storage layout that loses any of these surfaces is not a lawful\nMarkov-object storage layout.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F10.%20Markov-object%20overlay%20construction%2FStorage%20shape",
          "start_line":1013
        }
      ],
      "key":"overlay_storage_requirements",
      "statement":"Store a package attached to the entity cut, not merely a table row or membership list. Retain all six surfaces: space/version; direction/support; ledger evidence pointers; treatment/context/outcome verification trace; who accepted and assurance basis; and supersession record including any predecessor. Losing any surface is unlawful. Query/projection conveniences cannot substitute for this package.",
      "uncertainty":"No concrete file or database layout is prescribed."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys":["attribute_ledger","builder_project","entity_cut"],
      "conditions":[],
      "exceptions":["Sparse first publication remains lawful under §9."],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1030,
          "quote":"Sufficient saturation means: materially important\nattributes have traceable support; remaining gaps are explicit\nambiguities rather than silent misses; and the resulting object cut is\nstable enough to publish and supersede later if needed.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F11.%20Saturation%2C%20composition%20and%20projection%2FSaturation%20law",
          "start_line":1025
        }
      ],
      "key":"ledger_saturation",
      "statement":"Construction is iterative; builders may repeatedly work a bounded source-object set until judged sufficiently saturated. Sufficiency requires traceable materially important attributes, explicit residual gaps rather than silent misses, and a cut stable enough to publish and later supersede. Silent unsupported attribute creation is unlawful.",
      "uncertainty":"Sufficiency is bounded to the source set and claim, not exhaustive knowledge."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys":["world_model","world_model_unit_catalog"],
      "conditions":[],
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1043,
          "quote":"profile-level mesh law should be ratified only\nonce the reusable node and edge model is stable",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F11.%20Saturation%2C%20composition%20and%20projection%2FComposition%20law",
          "start_line":1042
        }
      ],
      "key":"world_model_composition",
      "statement":"Build local published artifacts and cuts before stitching; do not begin with a central monolith. Composition preserves fragment authority, bounded-context meaning, treatment semantics, declared loss and ambiguity, without erasing source artifacts. A federated mesh is preferred to a flattened enterprise model. Detailed topology may remain product-local while developing; profile mesh law should wait for stable reusable nodes and edges.",
      "uncertainty":"The reusable mesh model and ratification are not supplied as settled."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys":["world_model","world_model_unit_catalog","published_semantic_layer"],
      "conditions":[],
      "exceptions":["Traceability includes treatments, covariance, adjoints and temporal references where applicable."],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1058,
          "quote":"`world model -> API contract -> schema contract`.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F11.%20Saturation%2C%20composition%20and%20projection%2FProjection%20law",
          "start_line":1055
        }
      ],
      "key":"world_model_projection",
      "statement":"Projection is downstream convenience, never semantic authority over the primary kernel. All projections should trace to governing objects, evidence and applicable treatment/covariance/adjoint/temporal artifacts. Tables, schemas, APIs, mapping documents and covariant transforms publish the same kernel. Because APIs usually carry more business semantics than bare schemas, world model→API contract→schema contract is preferred. Query/traversal may be first-class delivery without becoming the constitutional core.",
      "uncertainty":"The preferred order is not an exclusive pipeline requirement."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys":["world_model_planes"],
      "conditions":["Accepted understanding can be compiled for large-scale data movement."],
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1082,
          "quote":"They should not be the\nrow-by-row execution engine for large-scale data movement when the\nsemantic understanding has already been accepted and can be compiled",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F12.%20Planes%2C%20proof%20and%20development%2FControl%20plane%20and%20data%20plane",
          "start_line":1079
        }
      ],
      "key":"probabilistic_execution_preference",
      "statement":"LLMs and other probabilistic systems belong primarily on the semantic control plane and should assist comprehension, candidate alignment, ambiguity reduction and ranking. Under the stated scale/compilability condition they should not provide row-by-row execution.",
      "uncertainty":"The source states should, not an unconditional prohibition on all probabilistic execution."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys":["world_model_profile","world_model"],
      "conditions":[],
      "exceptions":["Additional compilation demonstration is recommended where the line is mature enough."],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1103,
          "quote":"The proof obligation is practical: build the world model\nonce, then show that the same semantic substrate can emit the legacy\nartifacts the organisation expects and the richer covariant outputs",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F12.%20Planes%2C%20proof%20and%20development%2FProof%20law",
          "start_line":1097
        }
      ],
      "key":"world_model_practical_proof",
      "statement":"Adoption should not wait for winning standardisation. The preferred wedge is comprehend one bounded slice, publish one fragment, stitch one adjacent fragment, answer one painful question incumbent pipelines cannot cleanly answer, and emit conventional/covariant outputs side by side. This is incremental capture, not immediate central convergence. Practical proof demonstrates both legacy and richer outputs from one substrate; mature lines should also demonstrate deterministic compilation retaining traceability and challengeability.",
      "uncertainty":"No such proof is performed by this interpretation."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys":["world_model","world_model_profile"],
      "conditions":[],
      "exceptions":["Simpler lines may use world model→application projections→implementation."],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1122,
          "quote":"Use\nnormative application specs where the problem is primarily user\ninteraction, workflow choice, non-domain behaviour, or operational policy\nbeyond the domain semantics themselves.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F12.%20Planes%2C%20proof%20and%20development%2FWorld-model-driven%20development",
          "start_line":1117
        }
      ],
      "key":"world_model_development_allocation",
      "statement":"World-model-driven development parallels spec-driven work: specs are usually normative and models usually descriptive. A sufficiently formed model can project substantial applications without duplicated semantic authorship. Preferred relationship is model→epistemic correspondence overlay→deterministic compiled artifacts→implementation. Use normative application specs for primarily interaction, workflow choice, non-domain behaviour or extra-domain operational policy; use the model substrate where software mainly interfaces to stable domain reality.",
      "uncertainty":"Usually and can do not establish universal identities or guaranteed generative coverage."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys":["world_model_result_domains"],
      "conditions":[],
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1173,
          "quote":"Each refinement names\nthe question it answers and the predicate its mapping is for, and maps\neach of its values to exactly one core value.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F14.%20Results%20of%20this%20profile",
          "start_line":1167
        }
      ],
      "key":"world_model_result_mapping",
      "statement":"Values map exactly once to core for their own predicates, without standing promotion or cross-predicate satisfaction. Cut: cut_admissible→satisfied for each stated/traced/discriminated surface, including reasoned non-applicability and bounded sparse publication with residual ambiguity; cut_inadmissible→falsified for missing lawful value, missing trace or evidenced undiscriminated alternative, naming the counterexample; discrimination_undecided→indeterminate only absent such counterexample when evidence cannot decide claimed discrimination, naming needed evidence. Direction: direction_verified→satisfied requires admissible extraction in declared space, recorded acceptable held-out preservation and no recorded identity loss; extraction_inadmissible→falsified for PCA/maximum variance regardless of verification; verification_failed→falsified for admissible extraction with recorded identity loss; verification_inconclusive→indeterminate for admissible extraction in declared space with a run deciding neither preservation nor loss and no other run establishing either, naming deciding verification; representation_space_invalid→invalid_basis for no declared space or cross-space composition absent extraction/failure counterexample. Publication: published_verified→satisfied for recorded acceptable verification; published_unverified→falsified for publication without it. Storage: storage_retained→satisfied for all six package surfaces; storage_lossy→falsified naming any lost surface. Null peers: null_peer_discriminated→satisfied for unique identity-loaded core and cleaner-than-random transfer; not_yet_lawful→falsified for either test failure. Gate: gate_met→satisfied or gate_not_met→falsified only for the run, leaving construct standing unchanged on failure. Saturation: saturated→satisfied for supported material attributes, explicit gaps and stable cut, carrying residuals; not_saturated→falsified names failed support/gap/stability condition. Otherwise indeterminate names needed evidence, out_of_frame concerns undeclared required relation/capability, and invalid_basis covers unsupported subject/basis other than representation_space_invalid.",
      "uncertainty":"These mappings describe possible source-defined results; none is assigned to an actual evaluated artifact."
    },
